THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the constructor doesn’t initialize the transient iterator fields (entries1/2, values1/2, keys1/2) on all paths. They’re currently left null and lazily created elsewhere, but NullAway expects them to be non-null. The safest fix is to eagerly initialize them in the constructor after the tables are allocated, using the existing inner classes, ensuring no early-return path skips initialization.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '113a\ \ \ \ entries1 = new Entries(this);
    entries2 = new Entries(this);
    values1 = new Values(this);
    values2 = new Values(this);
    keys1 = new Keys(this);
    keys2 = new Keys(this);' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/ObjectFloatMap.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | head && tail -n 20 new_build_output.log
```

